# Top-level Eclipse/MCUXpresso project metadata auto-created when this
# folder gets opened/indexed by the IDE. Not real project content.
/.project

# demo_code/02_uart_hello_world_reference is intentionally source-only
# (see Section 9: "try this yourself before opening the reference folder").
# MCUXpresso can auto-generate a broken external-build .project/.cproject
# pair for it (managedBuildOn=false, no real Makefile behind it), which
# causes "make: *** No rule to make target `all'" if anyone tries to
# build it directly. Don't track those if they reappear.
demo_code/02_uart_hello_world_reference/.project
demo_code/02_uart_hello_world_reference/.cproject

# CMake-regenerated build files under each project's armgcc/ folder.
# These embed machine-specific absolute paths (CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR,
# CMAKE_BINARY_DIR, compiler paths) and get freshly regenerated by
# `cmake` on any machine, so committing them just ships someone else's
# local paths. CMakeLists.txt itself is hand-maintained and IS tracked.
**/armgcc/CMakeCache.txt
**/armgcc/CMakeFiles/
**/armgcc/cmake_install.cmake
**/armgcc/Makefile
**/armgcc/debug/
